<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Lumos - android-app/app / Lint scoping for the two kinds of test source.
  Author: dhar.abhishek.email@gmail.com
  Implements: TRS-CODE-006, TRS-AND-001
  ADRs: -
  Threading: n/a
  Notes: build.gradle.kts turns on checkTestSources, and this file is what makes
  that setting correct rather than merely strict.

  The module has two test source sets and they run on different runtimes:

    src/androidTest  runs ON A DEVICE, at minSdk. NewApi applies exactly as it
                     does to production code - S4b proved it, with an
                     InputStream.readAllBytes call that was green on a local API
                     34 emulator and threw NoSuchMethodError on the API 30 image
                     the pipeline uses.
    src/test         runs on the HOST JVM, at Java 21. It never sees an Android
                     runtime, so "requires API level 33" is a statement about a
                     platform this code will never execute on. Files.readAllBytes,
                     Stream.toList and ByteArrayOutputStream.writeBytes are all
                     ordinary JDK 21 and all correct where they are.

  So NewApi is suppressed for src/test ONLY, by path, and stays live everywhere
  else including src/androidTest. Every other lint check remains active in both.
  A blanket checkTestSources = false would have been the easy alternative and is
  what let the S4b bug through.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="NewApi">
        <ignore path="src/test" />
    </issue>
</lint>
